<title>DENMARK: Denmark's Phoenix soars on takeover bid.</title>
<headline>Denmark's Phoenix soars on takeover bid.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish roadmaker Phoenix contractors soared by close to six percent on Thursday after a public offer for its shares by construction heavyweight Superfos.</p>
<p>At 1115 GMT Phoenix C-shares traded at 625 crowns, up from Wednesday's closing 590.</p>
<p>Superfos is offering 625 crowns apiece for the shares and 700 crowns for each A-share, trumping an offer from Norway's Rieber and Son of 650 Danish crowns for the A-share and 585 for the C-share.</p>
<p>-- Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
</text>
